name: downtown-redevelopment
version: 1.0.0
profile: geostory
description: How San Francisco rebuilt the forty acres around its bus terminal

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A planning-department story: a real redevelopment area, told from the ground.
#
# This example exists to exercise the parts of the format the others do not -
# the basemaps and annotations registries, per-scene layer visibility, and a
# 3D camera request that a 2D renderer must degrade rather than reject.
#
# Every place here is real and every coordinate resolves. An example that
# invents a city while claiming a high-confidence geocode teaches the opposite
# of what the places registry is for.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

story:
  title: "Rebuilding Transbay"
  author: "Urban Planning Department"
  crs: "EPSG:4326"
  tags: ["urban planning", "transit", "san francisco", "redevelopment"]

settings:
  default_basemap: bm_streets
  default_duration: 10
  default_transition: fly
  camera_3d_degradation: 3d_degradation_wide_shot
  loop: false

basemaps:
  - id: bm_streets
    name: "CartoDB Positron"
    type: xyz
    url: "https://basemaps.cartocdn.com/light_all/{z}/{x}/{y}.png"
    max_zoom: 20
    attribution: "© OpenStreetMap contributors © CARTO"

  - id: bm_aerial
    name: "Esri World Imagery"
    type: xyz
    url: "https://server.arcgisonline.com/ArcGIS/rest/services/World_Imagery/MapServer/tile/{z}/{y}/{x}"
    max_zoom: 19
    attribution: "© Esri, Maxar, Earthstar Geographics"

places:
  - id: pl_transbay
    as_written: "the Transbay district"
    resolved:
      name: "Transbay, San Francisco, California"
      point: [-122.3948, 37.7887]
      bounds: [[-122.4005, 37.7845], [-122.3890, 37.7925]]
      kind: region
      provider: nominatim
      resolved_at: "2026-08-21T00:00:00Z"
      confidence: 0.88

  - id: pl_transit_center
    as_written: "Salesforce Transit Center"
    resolved:
      name: "Salesforce Transit Center, San Francisco"
      point: [-122.3969, 37.7896]
      bounds: [[-122.4005, 37.7889], [-122.3936, 37.7903]]
      kind: landmark
      provider: nominatim
      resolved_at: "2026-08-21T00:00:00Z"
      confidence: 0.96

  - id: pl_salesforce_tower
    as_written: "Salesforce Tower"
    resolved:
      name: "Salesforce Tower, San Francisco"
      point: [-122.3968, 37.7897]
      kind: landmark
      provider: nominatim
      resolved_at: "2026-08-21T00:00:00Z"
      confidence: 0.97

  - id: pl_rincon_hill
    as_written: "Rincon Hill"
    resolved:
      name: "Rincon Hill, San Francisco, California"
      point: [-122.3899, 37.7857]
      bounds: [[-122.3945, 37.7830], [-122.3855, 37.7880]]
      kind: region
      provider: nominatim
      resolved_at: "2026-08-21T00:00:00Z"
      confidence: 0.90

# Narration is text. Nothing here names a recording, because there is not one
# and there does not need to be - see the core invariant in the README.
audio: []
media: []

layers:
  - id: lyr_plan_area
    name: "Transbay Redevelopment Project Area"
    type: geojson
    source: "layers/transbay-project-area.geojson"
    style:
      color: "#1D4ED8"
      fill_opacity: 0.12
      weight: 2

  - id: lyr_height_limits
    name: "Height and Bulk Districts"
    type: geojson
    source: "layers/height-limits.geojson"
    style:
      color: "#B45309"
      fill_opacity: 0.2
      weight: 1

annotations:
  - id: ann_walk_radius
    kind: circle
    geometry: { type: Point, coordinates: [-122.3969, 37.7896] }
    radius_m: 800
    label: "Ten minutes on foot"
    style:
      color: "#0F766E"
      fill_color: "#0F766E"
      fill_opacity: 0.1
      weight: 2

  - id: ann_bus_ramp
    kind: line
    geometry:
      type: LineString
      coordinates:
        - [-122.3903, 37.7908]
        - [-122.3931, 37.7902]
        - [-122.3958, 37.7898]
    label: "Elevated bus ramp from the Bay Bridge"
    style:
      color: "#B91C1C"
      weight: 3

  - id: ann_tower_site
    kind: marker
    geometry: { type: Point, coordinates: [-122.3968, 37.7897] }
    label: "Salesforce Tower — 326 m"
    style:
      color: "#111827"

scenes:
  - id: sc_01_terminal
    sequence: 1
    title: "What Was There"
    place_id: pl_transbay
    basemap: bm_streets
    transition: cut
    timing: { mode: derived, intended: 13 }
    layers_visible: [lyr_plan_area]
    content:
      caption: "The Transbay Terminal, 1939 to 2010."
      narration: >-
        For seventy years this corner of downtown San Francisco was organised
        around a bus terminal. The Transbay Terminal opened in nineteen
        thirty-nine to receive electric trains from across the Bay Bridge, and
        when the trains stopped running it was converted to buses and slowly
        surrounded by parking lots and freeway ramps.

  - id: sc_02_plan_area
    sequence: 2
    title: "The Project Area"
    place_id: pl_transbay
    basemap: bm_streets
    transition: fly
    timing: { mode: derived, intended: 12 }
    layers_visible: [lyr_plan_area, lyr_height_limits]
    content:
      caption: "Roughly forty acres, replanned as one piece."
      narration: >-
        The redevelopment plan treated the whole district as a single project
        rather than a series of parcels. Publicly owned land freed up by
        demolishing the old freeway ramps was sold to help fund the new transit
        centre, and height limits were raised in a ring that steps down as it
        moves away from it.

  - id: sc_03_walkshed
    sequence: 3
    title: "Ten Minutes on Foot"
    place_id: pl_transit_center
    basemap: bm_streets
    transition: fly
    timing: { mode: derived, intended: 11 }
    annotation_ids: [ann_walk_radius, ann_bus_ramp]
    content:
      caption: "Density was allocated by walking distance."
      narration: >-
        Everything was measured from the front door of the transit centre. The
        tallest towers were allowed closest to it, and the ring drawn here is
        roughly eight hundred metres, about ten minutes on foot. The red line
        is the elevated ramp that brings buses in directly from the bridge.

  - id: sc_04_transit_center
    sequence: 4
    title: "The New Centre"
    place_id: pl_transit_center
    basemap: bm_aerial
    transition: dissolve
    timing: { mode: derived, intended: 14 }
    content:
      caption: "Opened 2018, closed six weeks later, reopened 2019."
      narration: >-
        The Salesforce Transit Center opened in August twenty eighteen and shut
        again six weeks later, when cracks were found in two steel beams over
        Fremont Street. It reopened the following July, after the beams were
        repaired and the design independently reviewed. Below it sits an empty
        train box, built for rail service that has not yet been funded.

  - id: sc_05_park
    sequence: 5
    title: "The Roof"
    place_id: pl_transit_center
    basemap: bm_aerial
    transition: fly
    timing: { mode: fixed, intended: 10 }
    content:
      caption: "Salesforce Park — 5.4 acres, four storeys up."
      narration: >-
        The roof is a public park: five and a half acres of gardens running the
        full length of the building, about twenty metres above the street. It
        is the part of the project people actually use every day.

  - id: sc_06_tower
    sequence: 6
    title: "The Tower"
    place_id: pl_salesforce_tower
    basemap: bm_aerial
    transition: fly
    timing: { mode: derived, intended: 11 }
    annotation_ids: [ann_tower_site]
    camera:
      mode: 3d
      center: [-122.3968, 37.7897]
      zoom: 17
      pitch: 55
      bearing: 20
    content:
      caption: "326 metres, and part of how the terminal was paid for."
      narration: >-
        Salesforce Tower rises three hundred and twenty-six metres beside the
        transit centre, the tallest building in San Francisco. The land beneath
        it was sold by the transit authority, and that sale is a significant
        part of how the terminal below was funded.

  - id: sc_07_rincon
    sequence: 7
    title: "Down the Hill"
    place_id: pl_rincon_hill
    basemap: bm_streets
    transition: fly
    timing: { mode: derived, intended: 12 }
    layers_visible: [lyr_height_limits]
    layers_hidden: [lyr_plan_area]
    content:
      caption: "Rincon Hill absorbed the housing."
      narration: >-
        South of the transit centre, Rincon Hill was rezoned from light
        industry to high-density housing, and thousands of homes were built on
        blocks that had held warehouses and freeway approaches. Towers there
        were required to contribute towards affordable housing elsewhere in the
        district.

  - id: sc_08_now
    sequence: 8
    title: "Twenty Years On"
    place_id: pl_transbay
    basemap: bm_aerial
    transition: dissolve
    timing: { mode: derived, intended: 11 }
    layers_visible: [lyr_plan_area]
    content:
      caption: "A district built around a building that is not finished."
      narration: >-
        Two decades after the plan was adopted, the skyline is built and the
        streets are rebuilt, while the railway the whole thing was designed
        around remains a proposal. Whether Transbay reads as a success depends
        largely on whether the trains ever arrive.

attribution:
  - "© OpenStreetMap contributors © CARTO"
  - "© Esri, Maxar, Earthstar Geographics"
